B.YO=new A.cw("Everything so far you typed yourself. `input()` is how a program pauses and waits for the person using it.",null)
B.Z4=new A.cw("Anything you put in the brackets is shown as the question. Python stops there, waits, and hands back whatever they answer.","name = input('What is your name? ')")
B.Z0=new A.cw("Whatever comes back is always **text**, even if they type a number. That's why it goes straight into `name` \u2014 and why you can print it with a greeting.","name = input('What is your name? ')\nprint('Hello', name)")
B.Z7=new A.cw("Now your program reacts to the person running it. In the next step you can try it \u2014 this one needs the keyboard.",null)
B.a_L=s([B.YO,B.Z4,B.Z0,B.Z7],t.xu)
B.Zk=new A.kf(B.a_L)
